It&#x27;s my common code review comment to the beginners to not embed structs. There&#x27;s rarely anything to be gained by doing so. The only use case I found to be useful is to embed something like:<p><pre><code>    type MockHandlers struct {
        UnimplementedHandlers
    }

    func (m MockServer) LoginHandler{ &#x2F;* ... *&#x2F; }
</code></pre>
where I get to override only a part of a bigger interface at a time and have the embedding take care of the rest by saying panic(&quot;unimplemented&quot;) to satisfy the interface.
